thousand_ways#:#1000 ways Forum
thousand_ways_info#:#Every member (except the lecturers) randomly gets one of four roles for how to discuss in the forum: Hakutaku (facts), Kitsune (questioning), Tanuki (examples) or Kodama (connecting and mediating). The roles are distributed evenly; lecturers can change or reshuffle them in the tab “Members”.
thousand_ways_role#:#1000-ways role
creature_your_role#:#Your role: %s (%s) – %s
creature_hakutaku#:#Hakutaku
creature_hakutaku_role#:#The fact finder
creature_hakutaku_hint#:#Like the all-knowing white beast, you bring facts into the discussion: definitions, figures and sources. For example: “According to the script …”, “The definition is …”, “Source: …”.
creature_kitsune#:#Kitsune
creature_kitsune_role#:#The questioner
creature_kitsune_hint#:#Like the clever fox, you look behind things: ask for reasons, point out contradictions and gaps. For example: “How do we know that?”, “Does this also hold if …?”, “What speaks against it?”.
creature_tanuki#:#Tanuki
creature_tanuki_role#:#The example giver
creature_tanuki_hint#:#Like the shape-shifting raccoon dog, you make abstract things tangible: with examples, comparisons and everyday situations. For example: “Imagine …”, “An everyday example: …”, “In concrete terms …”.
creature_kodama#:#Kodama
creature_kodama_role#:#The connector
creature_kodama_hint#:#Like the tree spirit carrying the echo through the forest, you connect: link posts, summarise, look for common ground and mediate. For example: “If I combine A and B …”, “You both actually mean …”, “In summary: …”.
reshuffle#:#Reshuffle
confirm_reshuffle#:#Do you want to distribute the roles of all members anew at random? The current assignment will be lost.
roles_saved#:#The roles have been saved.
roles_reshuffled#:#The roles have been reshuffled.
